[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Requirements Data
PREFIX: HLR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Verifier Component Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-001
TITLE: Execution Log Loading
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall load execution logs from JSON files and parse them into in-memory
structures for comparison against test case definitions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-002
TITLE: Output Pattern Matching
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall compare actual output against expected patterns using exact match,
regex match, and JSON schema validation strategies.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-003
TITLE: Exit Code Verification
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall verify step exit codes match expected values with optional range
or set matching.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-004
TITLE: Detailed Mismatch Reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
When verification fails, the verifier shall report expected vs actual values with
character-level highlighting of differences.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-VER-005
TITLE: Batch Verification Orchestration
STATEMENT: >>>
The verifier shall orchestrate verification of multiple execution logs with aggregated
pass/fail counts and summary statistics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-VER-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Case Content Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-001
TITLE: Test Case Parsing
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall parse test case YAML files extracting test_case_id, title,
sequences, steps, and metadata fields.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-002
TITLE: Sequence Organization
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall organize test steps into sequences with proper scoping of
variables and execution order guarantees.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-003
TITLE: Step Command Storage
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall store and retrieve test step commands with command metadata
(description, expected output, exit code).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-004
TITLE: Variable Capture Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall support regex-based and command-based variable capture with
specification of variable names and extraction patterns.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-005
TITLE: Expected Output Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall support configurable expected output with match type (exact, regex,
schema), comparison values, and optional flags.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-006
TITLE: Prerequisite Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall manage test prerequisites with type (manual/automatic), description,
verification commands, and completion status.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-007
TITLE: Environment Variable Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall manage required and optional environment variables with defaults,
validation, and substitution into test commands.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-TC-008
TITLE: Hook Point Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall support configurable lifecycle hooks at eight execution points with
command specifications and error handling behavior.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-TC-008

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: YAML Input/Output Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-001
TITLE: YAML Schema Resolution
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall extract the schema field from YAML files and resolve it to the
appropriate JSON schema file for validation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-002
TITLE: YAML Type Detection
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall extract the type field from YAML files to identify the content
type for appropriate processing and validation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-003
TITLE: Test Case YAML Loading
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall deserialize test case YAML to TestCase structures with proper
handling of all supported fields and nesting.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-004
TITLE: Execution Log JSON Escaping
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall properly escape command output for JSON encoding using jq, custom
escaper, or shell fallback methods.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-005
TITLE: Verification Result YAML Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall serialize verification results to YAML format with structured
output for all test sequences and steps.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-006
TITLE: Container YAML Generation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall generate container YAML aggregating test metadata and verification
results for documentation generation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-YAML-007
TITLE: YAML Round-trip Preservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall preserve test case information through YAML load/save cycles
without loss or modification.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-YAML-007

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Test Schema Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-001
TITLE: Schema File Management
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall load, cache, and serve JSON schema files for validation with
proper error handling for missing or malformed schemas.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-002
TITLE: Schema Constraint Enforcement
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall validate YAML content against schema constraints including required
fields, type constraints, and value restrictions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-003
TITLE: Nested Structure Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall recursively validate nested objects (sequences, steps, verifications)
against their schema definitions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-004
TITLE: Pattern Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall validate regex patterns and variable name formats against predefined
patterns to ensure syntactic correctness.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-005
TITLE: Enumeration Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall validate enumerated field values against allowed enum sets defined
in the schema.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-006
TITLE: Execution Log Schema Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall use execution log schema to validate JSON execution output structure
and required fields.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-007
TITLE: Verification Result Schema Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall use verification result schema to validate container YAML structure
and compatibility.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-SCHEMA-008
TITLE: Validation Error Reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
The software shall report validation errors with specific field paths, constraint type,
expected value, and actual value.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SCHEMA-008

[[/SECTION]]
